# Call-site ledger of avro at sha256:e900e7b59a4781f63d9e935e88f6ec50c4d60be3f4adf9c63b51ed39d578fe08.
# Decide every `undecided` line; see macro-benchmark/README.md.
#
# Hand-written from the source of the sdist avro-1.12.2.tar.gz; the judgements
# are in avro.md. avro 1.12.2 declares requires-python >= 3.10 and the
# classifiers CPython 3.10 to 3.14, no implementation and no operating system:
# the admitted runtimes are CPython 3.10 and later (3.15 included; the last
# classifier is no upper bound). python-snappy and zstandard are optional
# extras that the test environment does not install: their calls are named as
# missing modules (snappy.*, zstandard.*).
default reject avro.schema.Schema.__eq__: Schema.__eq__ is abstract and every concrete schema class takes __eq__ from EqualByPropsMixin or EqualByJsonMixin, which come before Schema in its MRO (PrimitiveSchema, FixedSchema, EnumSchema and their logical subclasses: EqualByPropsMixin; ArraySchema, MapSchema, UnionSchema, ErrorUnionSchema, RecordSchema: EqualByJsonMixin); nothing calls Schema.__eq__ explicitly
default reject avro.schema.EqualByJsonMixin.__eq__, avro.schema.EqualByPropsMixin.__eq__, avro.name.Name.__eq__, avro.protocol.Message.__eq__, avro.protocol.Protocol.__eq__, avro.compatibility.ReaderWriter.__eq__: no operand of this comparison or `in` test, and no key of this dict or set operation, is a schema, field, Name, Message, Protocol or ReaderWriter: the operands and keys are strs (type names, field and symbol names, namespaces), SchemaType members (str's == and hash), ints, bytes, bools, None, lists, tuples, dicts of JSON values, typing constructs and client values; the sites where package code compares such an object or uses it as a key accept these methods explicitly
default reject avro.schema.EqualByJsonMixin.__hash__, avro.schema.EqualByPropsMixin.__hash__, avro.compatibility.ReaderWriter.__hash__: no schema, field or ReaderWriter is hashed at this site: the hashed keys and set or dict elements are strs, SchemaType members, ints, bytes, tuples, typing constructs and client values; the memo map of ReaderWriterCompatibilityChecker, keyed by ReaderWriter, accepts ReaderWriter.__hash__ explicitly
default reject avro.datafile.DataFileReader.__iter__, avro.datafile.DataFileReader.__next__: no DataFileReader is iterated, unpacked or searched with `in` here: the iterables are lists, tuples, dicts and their views, sets, strs, bytes, ranges, generators, schema field and branch lists, *args tuples and client values; the sites that iterate a DataFileReader (avro.__main__.print_avro, avro.tool.main_dump, the next() calls of avro.tool) accept them explicitly
default reject avro.protocol.Message.errors: the receiver of this attribute load is not a Message: almost every load of `errors` is the module avro.errors on the package avro (avro.errors.X); the loads of .errors on a Message (ipc, protocol) accept it explicitly
default reject avro.schema.Schema.__str__, avro.schema.Field.__str__, avro.protocol.Protocol.__str__, avro.protocol.Message.__str__, avro.compatibility.SchemaType.__str__: no schema, field, Protocol, Message or SchemaType member is formatted, printed or converted to str here: the formatted values are strs, ints, bytes, Decimals, dates, exceptions, dicts and lists of JSON values, Names' strs, sets of strs and client values; the sites that format or convert such an object accept them explicitly
default reject avro.datafile._DataFileMetadata.schema: the receiver of this attribute load or store is not a DataFileReader or DataFileWriter: almost every load of `schema` is the module avro.schema on the package avro (avro.schema.X) or a local variable or parameter; the loads and stores of .schema on a data file accept it explicitly
default reject avro.name.Name.name, avro.protocol.Message.name, avro.protocol.Protocol.name, avro.schema.NamedSchema.name: the receiver of this attribute load does not have this property: a Field (instance attribute name), a GenericResponder's or TaskRunnerResponder's message (accepted where the receiver is a Message), an argparse namespace, a file, or a client value; the loads on a Name, NamedSchema, Message or Protocol accept these properties explicitly

